 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "Six reasons nobody can copy Israel."
  },
  {
   "say": "In nineteen ninety, Michael Porter drew a diamond that explains why countries win.",
   "screen": "Porter's Diamond, *1990*",
   "at": "L1",
   "until": "L2"
  },
  {
   "say": "Corner one, people. Half of adults have a degree, and army tech units train them young.",
   "screen": "Factor conditions: *people*",
   "at": "L2",
   "until": "L3"
  },
  {
   "say": "Corner two, demand. Ten million people is a tiny market, so startups go global from day one.",
   "screen": "Demand: a *tiny* home market",
   "at": "L3",
   "until": "L4e"
  },
  {
   "say": "That's why high tech is fifty eight percent of exports."
  },
  {
   "say": "Corner three, the cluster. Over five hundred multinationals have set up here since two thousand.",
   "screen": "Related industries: *the cluster*",
   "at": "L5",
   "until": "L6"
  },
  {
   "say": "Corner four, rivalry. About seven hundred fifty new tech companies a year, all fighting for talent.",
   "screen": "Rivalry: *750* new companies a year",
   "at": "L6",
   "until": "L7"
  },
  {
   "say": "Then two outside forces. Government: in nineteen ninety three, Yozma put one hundred million dollars into venture capital.",
   "screen": "Government: *Yozma,* 1993",
   "at": "L7",
   "until": "L8e"
  },
  {
   "say": "Today, six point three five percent of the economy goes to research. Highest among developed countries."
  },
  {
   "say": "And chance. When the Soviet Union fell, almost nine hundred thousand people came, many of them engineers.",
   "screen": "Chance: the *Soviet* collapse",
   "at": "L9",
   "until": "L10"
  },
  {
   "say": "The weak spot? High tech is only about one in nine jobs.",
   "screen": "The *weak* spot",
   "at": "L10",
   "until": "L11"
  },
  {
   "say": "Six forces, feeding each other. That's why nobody can just copy Israel."
  }
 ],
